  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 103.33 Insignificant effect on environmental quality",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 103.33 “Insignificant effect on environmental quality” means a minimal adverse change in the quality of groundwater, surface water, air quality, or public health, either for the short term or the long term.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 103.29) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
